# This repo publishes under its own npm identity, not the machine's default one.
#
# npm keys auth by registry URL, so a token here overrides ~/.npmrc for this
# project only. The value is read from the environment on purpose: NEVER paste a
# literal token into this file, it is committed.
#
# If SUNO_CLIENT_NPM_TOKEN is unset, npm sends the unexpanded string and the
# publish fails 401. That is the desired failure: it cannot silently fall back
# to the machine's default account and publish under the wrong name.
//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${SUNO_CLIENT_NPM_TOKEN}
